00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.400
in which is useful to capital.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.060
And for desserts daughters,

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:20.790
Marx left social reproduction
out of the picture.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.730
And this not a focus on exploitation

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:27.770
would basically close off the analysis

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.330
of spaces of resistance,

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:33.130
which is my colleague argument.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:37.900
And for Nancy Fraser
echoed by Debbie Harvey,

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:41.210
we would need to expand the understanding

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:43.610
of anticapitalist struggles beyond

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:46.100
the traditional Marxist Canon

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:51.100
and so look not just to struggles
between labor and capital

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:54.470
at the point of production,

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:58.500
but also at boundary struggles
of agenda domination,

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.683
ecology, imperialism, and democracy.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:07.540
And my argument today is that
Capital is not really a book

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:11.360
about capital, but it's
a book against capital.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.460
And in the last instance,

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:17.580
it's a book that analyzes the antagonism

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.340
between two social systems,

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.640
so between capitalism and communism.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.860
And not seeing these from
my point of view results

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.220
from the same refined processes,

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:33.220
that Marx sees a place in
the commodity fetishism.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:37.180
So in order to somehow de-fetishize

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:42.180
the reading of Capital,
I will look first start

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:50.310
by discussing Marx's concepts
of labor and exploitation

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.820
and I will argue that
these concepts are crucial

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:58.270
to these inter-capital's
emancipatory potential

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:01.210
and read it from the point
of view of the community

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:04.860
of three producers that Marx introduces

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:09.580
at the end of this section
on commodity fetishism.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.702
I will then explain why
from my point of view,

00:11:12.702 --> 00:11:16.700
the point on capital reproduction
is key to understanding

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:19.040
the global scope of Marx's analysis,

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:23.870
including imperialism
and social reproduction.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:28.100
And then we'll conclude by
discussing what this does as

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:32.050
about Marx's conception
of the class struggle

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:36.910
and social revolution, both
in the 19th century and today.

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:40.100
And before I start, I
need to make a promise

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.470
because many people believe that Marx

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:47.470
was analyzing 19th century
England in Capital Volume One

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:52.300
but there, Marx also says
that he is using England

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:57.300
as a model to analyze the
overall fantasies of capitalism

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.400
and I think this is an important point

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.400
that we need to bear in mind,

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:06.339
which helps also explain why
the more capitalism develops,

00:12:06.339 --> 00:12:10.260
the more relevant Marx's
analysis seems to be.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:13.387
It's because he's looking
at overall time disease

00:12:13.387 --> 00:12:17.263
and not just a specific historical model.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:23.830
Okay, so it's clear
that Marx devoted quite

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:28.260
a lot of attention in capital
to labor exploitation,

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.940
but one could ask whether this focus

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:34.110
on labor exploitation really closes off

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:36.190
spaces of resistance.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.880
And I think it's important
to bear in mind that

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:43.040
for Marx, labor is an organic metabolism

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.870
between humankind and nature

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.940
and from his point of view, contrary

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:50.490
to the classical economist was derived

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:56.490
from both labor and nature
not from labor alone.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:01.220
And by selling their labor
power workers transfer

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:04.680
onto capital, their whole living power.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:08.000
So they put these organic metabolism,

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:13.000
between humankind and nature
in the hands of capital

00:13:13.397 --> 00:13:18.397
and by doing so, really these
create a complete overthrowing

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:24.780
of the relationship between
humankind and nature

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:28.000
and this is why for Marx in proportion,

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:31.930
as capital accumulates,
the situation of the worker

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:36.710
be his payment high or
low must grow worse, yeah.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.390
So it's both a qualitative

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:43.763
and quantitative process
of impoverishment.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:49.850
So even assuming that workers
are paid what's necessary

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:54.500
to cover their subsistence
and reproduction costs,

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:58.530
the value of the wage for
max is always lower than

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:02.400
the value that work is for
use in the production process.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.200
And from the moment they
entered the hidden aboard

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:08.530
of production, capitalist
consume that level of power

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:13.530
with the exclusive goal of
expanding the surplus labor time

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:17.930
and increasing the
extraction of surplus value.

00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:21.720
And that's why the development
of the productive forces

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:25.500
aims at creating a uniform
and continuous time

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:30.490
of valorization that renders
labor and purely abstract

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:32.990
and mechanical activity.

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:37.517
So in volume one from my point of view,

00:14:37.517 --> 00:14:41.550
and I suggested reading the
chapters from corporation

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:44.320
to a large scale industry.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:48.720
So those chapters are just
describing historical stages

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.900
in the development of capitalism,

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:55.090
but are also highlighting the
fundamental contradictions

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.090
of such development.

00:14:57.090 --> 00:15:01.240
And Marx shows that
capitalism renders work

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:05.820
as source of mortification
rather than a human fulfillment

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:10.140
and that eating polishes
the workers turns them

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:13.590
into a fragment of themselves
and separates manual

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:17.030
and intellectual tasks and slaving science

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:18.140
on their capitals.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:22.690
So it's really an analysis of
the progressive subordination

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:27.533
of labor or substantiation
of labor under capital.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:33.370
And this process proceeds hand in hand

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:37.970
with the exploitation and
squandering of nature.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:40.220
And this is why from my point of view,

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:43.410
Marxist theory of exploitation concerns,

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:47.580
the totality of capitalists such relations

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:51.280
and has an important ecological dimension

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:55.970
that resonates today, for example
in the studies of scholars

00:15:55.970 --> 00:16:00.640
like Rob Wallace or John Bellamy, foster,

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.480
and other scholars who have shown that

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:07.260
the spread of pandemics like COVID-19,

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:11.690
are linked to industrial
agriculture and deforestation.

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:15.470
And so from this point of view, COVID-19

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:19.000
would therefore point to
the limits of capitalism

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:23.173
as an ecological and
ecological system as well.

