00:50:10.470 --> 00:50:15.470
So I liked it when a poet was reading some

00:50:16.540 --> 00:50:20.340
of the passages about the
importance of anti-colonial

00:50:20.340 --> 00:50:25.340
struggles in Marx already
in the early fifties,

00:50:25.680 --> 00:50:29.690
when Marx supported
uprisings in China and India

00:50:29.690 --> 00:50:31.900
against British colonialism,

00:50:31.900 --> 00:50:36.090
and actually believed that they
could either react on Europe

00:50:36.090 --> 00:50:40.630
and accelerate the tendency
towards crisis and revolution,

00:50:40.630 --> 00:50:42.390
or they could be the premise for

00:50:42.390 --> 00:50:45.900
the capitalist national
development of these countries.

00:50:45.900 --> 00:50:49.297
And Marx also followed
enthusiastically the development of

00:50:49.297 --> 00:50:51.990
the civil war in the United States.

00:50:51.990 --> 00:50:55.850
And as black abolitionists
like Frederick Douglas,

00:50:55.850 --> 00:50:58.090
he believed that the outcome of the war

00:50:58.090 --> 00:51:02.350
depended on the mobilization
of African Americans

00:51:02.350 --> 00:51:07.087
and therefore it depended on
the emancipation of the slaves.

00:51:07.087 --> 00:51:10.760
And this emancipation in
his view was the premise

00:51:10.760 --> 00:51:13.640
for any further progress
of the liberal movement

00:51:13.640 --> 00:51:16.690
because as it's well known
from his point of view,

00:51:16.690 --> 00:51:20.790
laboring white skin
cannot emancipate itself

00:51:20.790 --> 00:51:23.180
when it is branded in a black skin.

00:51:23.180 --> 00:51:26.430
And indeed the movement
for the eight hour day

00:51:26.430 --> 00:51:30.900
immediately grew in the U.S. after the end

00:51:30.900 --> 00:51:34.860
of the civil war and
then spread to Europe.

00:51:34.860 --> 00:51:37.290
So when Marx discusses the movement

00:51:37.290 --> 00:51:40.170
for the reduction of the
working day, he's not,

00:51:40.170 --> 00:51:42.760
it doesn't tell me mine
that pure class struggle

00:51:42.760 --> 00:51:46.140
that between bourgeoisie and proletariat

00:51:46.140 --> 00:51:50.870
that proceeds in linear ways
in separate national context

00:51:50.870 --> 00:51:53.400
but he has in mind is
international movement

00:51:53.400 --> 00:51:57.870
against both exploitation and oppression.

00:51:57.870 --> 00:51:59.780
At the end of the sixties,

00:51:59.780 --> 00:52:02.870
Marx changed his mind on the relationship

00:52:02.870 --> 00:52:06.537
between proletariat and
anti-colonial struggles.

00:52:06.537 --> 00:52:08.950
And so while initially in the manifesto,

00:52:08.950 --> 00:52:11.210
he proclaimed that social revolution

00:52:11.210 --> 00:52:15.360
was key to the liberation of
the colonies 10 years after,

00:52:15.360 --> 00:52:18.210
he was discussing with Angus, the dangers

00:52:18.210 --> 00:52:20.470
that Britain's exploitation of the word

00:52:20.470 --> 00:52:24.550
would create a bushwalk
proletariats silent or complicit

00:52:24.550 --> 00:52:26.730
with these domination.

00:52:26.730 --> 00:52:28.430
And at the end of the sixties,

00:52:28.430 --> 00:52:32.420
he concluded that independence
of Island was the premise

00:52:32.420 --> 00:52:35.560
for the emancipation of the
working class in England.

00:52:35.560 --> 00:52:39.240
So it was really in the
colonies that that was

00:52:39.240 --> 00:52:42.670
the key to the class
struggle even in the centers

00:52:42.670 --> 00:52:46.350
of the system and support
working class support

00:52:46.350 --> 00:52:49.850
for the independence of
Ireland was also the condition

00:52:49.850 --> 00:52:54.010
for causing the anti Irish
racism that was sparked

00:52:54.010 --> 00:52:56.523
